WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.690
A hillside weather station has exactly
one byte for the temperature: 8 bits.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.350
On a summer day at 20 degrees,
it stores zero zero zero one,

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.370
zero one zero zero.

4
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.290
Then, one winter night,
it drops to minus 20.

5
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.470
No spare bits, only 0s and 1s.

6
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.850
So where does the minus sign go?

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.690
In this mission, you'll see that 8
bits counting up from 0 hold 0 to 255,

8
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.430
with no minus sign.

9
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.970
You'll discover how one of those
bits could be given a new job.

10
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.330
And you'll meet two's complement,
the system computers mostly use.

11
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:42.200
Your mission: decide where the minus sign
goes in a one-byte thermometer at minus

12
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.280
20 degrees.
